# Changelog

All notable changes to `@re-cinq/hal-engine` are documented here.

The format is [Keep a Changelog 1.1.0](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/), and this project adheres to
[Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html). Entries are written for somebody installing the
package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.

## [Unreleased]

### Changed

- Tool input is now validated against the tool's declared `inputSchema` before its executor runs. A call the
  schema rejects returns the reason to the model as the tool result — naming the failing property path and the
  constraint it broke, never the offending value — instead of reaching your executor with malformed input.
  Valid input passes through unchanged: extra properties are kept, nothing is coerced and no defaults are
  applied, so input reaching an executor is already what the declared schema accepts. Executors that
  hand-validated or defensively cast their input can stop; a tool that relied on seeing malformed input to
  produce its own error message stops seeing it. Validation is done by `ajv`, which joins `dependencies`.


## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17

### Changed

